  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015): the contrast CT order is in, with the RBC-RAD-07 prep, a lab order and his instructions.\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001), linked to his Monday 10/26 9:00 appointment at St. Brigid (appt-t5-1026), as §5 requires.\n- **Allergy review:** St. Brigid's radiologist graded his 2019 iohexol reaction as moderate in the report that day: hives and eyelid swelling, no breathing problems. The \"anaphylaxis\" on his allergy list was added in 2021 from his own account, with no records reviewed. Per §1 that later label doesn't change the grade, so the \"no contrast\" rule for severe reactions (§3) doesn't apply. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies aren't risk factors under the policy.\n- **Premedication (§2):**\n  - Prednisone 50 mg by mouth Sunday 10/25 at 8 PM, then Monday 10/26 at 2 AM and 8 AM (mr-t0003, 3 tablets).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth Monday at 8 AM (mr-t0004, 1 capsule).\n  - He can't drive after the diphenhydramine and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney check (§4):** he needs a creatinine because he's 64 and has diabetes (on metformin). His last one, from 9/24, is 32 days before the scan, so it's outside the 30-day window. I ordered a new one (sr-t0002) to be drawn between today and Monday 8:30 AM, before the scan. No result exists yet.\n- **What I told him:** I sent him a portal message (comm-t0005) with:\n  - when to get the blood test\n  - the medication times, including the 2 AM dose\n  - that he must not drive and needs a ride\n  - that he should keep taking his usual medicines\n  - that prednisone may raise his blood sugar\n  - that he should tell imaging staff about the 2019 reaction\n  - to call 911 for hives, swelling or trouble breathing\n- **Follow-up:** I created an RN triage task (task-t0006, due Monday 8:30 AM) to make sure the creatinine is drawn and the result goes to you and St. Brigid. The task also covers calling him to confirm he got the instructions, picked up his medicines and has a driver. It escalates to you if either falls through.\n- **Chart note:** I wrote a progress note (doc-t0007) citing RBC-RAD-07.\n\nI didn't change his metformin, because RBC-RAD-07 doesn't cover it. You may want to decide that once the new creatinine is back.",
